WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:31.329
The search for sustainable development becomes

00:00:31.329 --> 00:00:34.050
the search for an adequate mode

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.630
of civilization

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.940
in the twenty-first

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.850
century. At the center of the idea of sustainability,
I think, is an ethical

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.870
imperative

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:49.010
to pass on an undiminished future

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.350
to our children.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.410
Well, no one is smart enough or can know enough

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:55.260
to predict

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.430
the future,

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:01.180
so if prediction is not a possibility,
then how can we make progress

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.230
in thinking about

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:07.550
our options, in thinking about our future
in an organized manner?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:14.550
And this is where scenario analysis comes
in.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.390
When we discuss scenarios,

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:25.210
we talk about three broad channels

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.460
radiating out into the future.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.220
One we call conventional worlds--

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.210
basically an evolutionary sequence of
events, despite hiccups like the current meltdown--

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:36.830
that the basic paradigm

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.390
and values

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:39.960
persist into the future.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.340
The second channel is barbarization, which is--

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.520
markets and policies are unable to cope with
the

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.770
crises

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:53.640
and the chaos and the social disruption and the environmental

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.550
deterioration that is induced by
conventional worlds.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:02.360
And you have futures of catastrophic disruption.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.309
And the third we call great transitions,

00:02:09.309 --> 00:02:12.430
where people rise to the

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:17.229
possibilities, to the promise of this planetary
phase with new values and new institutions

00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:20.430
and steer-- in developing, steers toward 

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.279
a more fortunate form of civilization.

00:02:24.279 --> 00:02:25.920
Two necessary

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.959
conditions

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:28.469
that must evolve

00:02:28.469 --> 00:02:33.129
to reach a civilization worth living in.

00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:40.879
Over the next ten years, we will see a wave

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:43.479
of engagement,

00:02:43.479 --> 00:02:44.329
and action,

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:45.930
of the citizens

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.499
of the world.

00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:53.759
I think the-- what I call, for shorthand,
a global citizens movement,

00:02:53.759 --> 00:02:56.400
is the necessary condition, the

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.869
necessary change agent,

00:02:58.869 --> 00:03:00.819
for a

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:01.679
turning

00:03:01.679 --> 00:03:03.190
away

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:06.829
from catastrophe, away from the abyss,

00:03:06.829 --> 00:03:07.549
toward

00:03:07.549 --> 00:03:09.099
Earthland,

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:11.249
this great transition future.

00:03:11.249 --> 00:03:13.879
I think that the

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:19.850
upsurge in civil society that we are seeing
now, and have seen for the last twenty years,

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:22.549
is a glimpse of what could

00:03:22.549 --> 00:03:24.099
occur. 

00:03:24.099 --> 00:03:26.729
But that civil society

00:03:26.729 --> 00:03:27.529
ferment

00:03:27.529 --> 00:03:29.770
is limited today

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.699
by fragmentation,

00:03:31.699 --> 00:03:33.579
by lack of a shared

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:36.430
vision of the possible.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:41.260
And I think this global citizens movement
is ready to be born, I think it's latent--

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.299
I think it could be brought to life.

00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:46.879
So that was the first area. I think the second area

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:51.159
is this:

00:03:51.159 --> 00:03:54.649
away from consumers and individualism and

00:03:54.649 --> 00:03:57.090
the domination of nature and

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.069
more towards questions of

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:01.790
the quality of life

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.809
and the 

00:04:05.809 --> 00:04:10.289
ecological sensibility and human solidarity--

00:04:10.289 --> 00:04:12.239
that would also be the second

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:12.760
pillar

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:16.269
that would signal that a shift

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:19.079
towards a great transition is possible.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.349
I think if we get to this livable future,

00:04:27.349 --> 00:04:32.910
it will be because humanity has found a way
to balance

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.019
the imperatives 

00:04:35.019 --> 00:04:37.680
of global responsibility

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.090
with diversity

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.509
and pluralism

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:42.919
and modes of culture

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:43.889
and development.

00:04:43.889 --> 00:04:47.150
When we take our trips to outer space,

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.479
and we look back, we see an

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:50.860
integral

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.119
blue planet.

00:04:52.119 --> 00:04:55.639
You don't see imaginary lines of states.

00:04:55.639 --> 00:05:02.639
And so that this globalism, this sense
of the earth as a natural unit

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.139
for a human

00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:07.039
organization and identity--

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:10.909
in some ways more profound

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:12.039
than

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:15.059
are the imaginary boundaries of

00:05:15.059 --> 00:05:21.939
of nation-state. When we look at the question
of value change that could undergird

00:05:21.939 --> 00:05:23.759
this great transition,

00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:26.599
I think we have to look at

00:05:26.599 --> 00:05:28.559
the process of change in

00:05:28.559 --> 00:05:33.460
two arenas: one in affluent countries
and one in developing countries.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:39.210
In affluent countries, we're already seeing
the precursors, the questioning of the meaning

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.699
of the good life.

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:47.459
Turning towards questions about the
quality of existence, not just the quantity

00:05:47.459 --> 00:05:48.280
of

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.479
things as defining success

00:05:51.479 --> 00:05:53.599
and well-being.

00:05:53.599 --> 00:05:54.899
So,

00:05:54.899 --> 00:05:56.710
that's one area-- is

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.529
a value change, is in terms of

00:05:59.529 --> 00:06:04.120
what it is to be a whole person and a fulfilled person.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:09.439
I think when we come to the question of the
developing world, there's an even more profound

00:06:09.439 --> 00:06:10.809
transition

00:06:10.809 --> 00:06:11.950
that we can imagine.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:17.619
To begin to define their own agenda for
development,

00:06:17.619 --> 00:06:22.069
that there are plural paths to modernity, not
a single path,

00:06:22.069 --> 00:06:25.979
and that their own paths can leapfrog a lot
of the mistakes

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:30.110
that have gone on in the industrialized
world,

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.629
and begin to come up

00:06:31.629 --> 00:06:38.349
with forms and models of development that
build on local traditions and customs

00:06:38.349 --> 00:06:40.430
and culture.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.500
Another area comes to

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.960
the question of the environment.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:50.449
People, I think, are coming to see that the
rapaciousness of the past

00:06:50.449 --> 00:06:51.990
must give way

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:55.289
to a sense of humanity's place

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:58.219
in the web of life.

00:06:58.219 --> 00:07:00.189
And dependence on its

00:07:00.189 --> 00:07:02.240
health, sustainability,

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:07.739
and bounty. So this is a major, almost Copernican
shift in awareness. 

00:07:07.739 --> 00:07:09.499
Copernicus

00:07:09.499 --> 00:07:10.460
taught us

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:15.199
that we didn't live at the center of the universe,
but that we were on a

00:07:15.199 --> 00:07:19.209
planet that revolved around the sun.

00:07:19.209 --> 00:07:24.349
Well, this new Copernican revolution,
I think, is telling us that we are not at the

00:07:24.349 --> 00:07:25.680
center of

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.449
Earth; we our part of the web

00:07:28.449 --> 00:07:31.650
of life of this grand ecology,

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:35.729
and if we don't take care to see our place
within it,

00:07:35.729 --> 00:07:42.729
then we may go down with it.

00:07:46.749 --> 00:07:49.930
I think there are three

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.569
major areas

00:07:51.569 --> 00:07:53.159
that we need to

00:07:53.159 --> 00:07:54.330
move down

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:57.830
to begin this transition.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.470
And those areas, I think, are understanding,

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:02.930
vision,

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:05.199
and action.

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:08.209
I think we need

00:08:08.209 --> 00:08:11.159
to gain a better grasp

00:08:11.159 --> 00:08:13.270
of this world we live in

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:16.669
and this emergent global system,

00:08:16.669 --> 00:08:19.300
both as scientists

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.379
and as citizens.

00:08:21.379 --> 00:08:25.229
We need to struggle,

00:08:25.229 --> 00:08:27.939
to expand our mental maps

00:08:27.939 --> 00:08:31.379
to traverse over space to take into account

00:08:31.379 --> 00:08:33.590
a global panorama.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:36.969
To span over time, to think over many decades,

00:08:36.969 --> 00:08:43.340
where people from all over the world can
find their place within this broad umbrella

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:47.640
that unifies their various concerns
into

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:54.640
a broad-based process of awareness-building
and political change

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.730
that can actually begin

00:08:56.730 --> 00:09:00.330
to steer things in a fundamentally different
direction.

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:07.330
So when we do reach our time of troubles-- which
well could come-- a time of systemic global crises,

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:11.140
that there is the political space and possibility

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:14.660
for recovery-- more than recovery

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:15.670
For building

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:16.740
and beginning

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:23.740
a new history.

